1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,258
Alexander wept because there were no worlds left to conquer... or did he?

2
00:00:06,508 --> 00:00:09,213
His mother said he was a son of Zeus.

3
00:00:09,263 --> 00:00:12,868
At twelve, he tamed a horse no man could ride.

4
00:00:12,918 --> 00:00:19,598
At Gordium, an oracle promised Asia to whoever untied a knot. He cut it with his sword.

5
00:00:19,648 --> 00:00:24,783
By thirty-two, he ruled from Greece to India, and never lost a battle.

6
00:00:24,933 --> 00:00:27,035
Or so the story goes.

7
00:00:27,185 --> 00:00:28,858
Let's start from the beginning.

8
00:00:28,908 --> 00:00:34,807
The battles are real: Issus, Gaugamela, the Hydaspes, all won.

9
00:00:34,857 --> 00:00:42,410
But the tears? Plutarch says he wept because the worlds were endless... and he didn't rule even one.

10
00:00:42,510 --> 00:00:48,797
And no Greek of his time called him "the Great." That name first appears in a Roman comedy.

11
00:00:48,947 --> 00:00:54,287
So was he great... or did Rome make him great?
